/t-nation.com/t/wanted-all-t-nation-members/57930","site":"T Nation · 655 posts · 2006"},{"title":"Why Can't Spock Get Men?","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/why-cant-spock-get-men/197209","site":"T Nation · 526 posts · 2014"},{"title":"Barley1 - 915 at 47","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/barley1-915-at-47/277997","site":"T Nation · 522 posts · 2022"},{"title":"Alpha Male Fashion","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/alpha-male-fashion/208928","site":"T Nation · 515 posts · 2015"},{"title":"Piece of ass of the year","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/piece-of-ass-of-the-year/28558","site":"T Nation · 331 posts · 2003"},{"title":"Skinny Bastards & Misconceptions","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/skinny-bastards-misconceptions/72474","site":"T Nation · 172 posts · 2006"}],"news":[],"social":[],"web":[{"title":"Boat shoe — Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boat_shoe"},{"title":"Boat shoe (Wikipedia)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boat_shoe"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Style & presentation","chain":["Moccasin-style leather or canvas shoe","Casual, nautical-preppy silhouette","More put-together summer outfit"],"effect":"direct","text":"Boat shoes dress down a smart-casual outfit with a classic, recognizable shape. Worn with shorts or chinos, they add a coastal, preppy touch."},"wikipedia":{"title":"Boat shoe","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boat_shoe"},"grokipedia":null,"lead":["Boat shoes, also called deck shoes or top-siders, are casual shoes in canvas or leather with a moccasin-style toe, durable stitching and non-marking rubber soles cut with grooves for grip on wet decks.[1]","Paul A. Sperry of New Haven, Connecticut, is credited with inventing the modern boat shoe in 1935 after noticing his dog ran on ice without slipping and cutting grooves into a sole; this led to the Sperry Top-Sider brand.[1]","People wear them for a relaxed nautical or preppy look. They have been everyday casual footwear in many coastal areas since the 1970s, trended in the 1980s and returned in the late 2000s.[1]"],"infobox":[["Type","Casual footwear"],["Invented","1935 (Paul A. Sperry)"],["Materials","Leather or canvas, rubber sole"],["Other names","Deck shoes, top-siders"],["Brands","Sperry, Sebago, Timberland, Eastland"]],"sections":[{"h":"Design","paras":["The shoe typically has oil-treated leather or canvas, moccasin construction, durable stitching and a grooved, non-marking sole intended for wet surfaces.[1] They are traditionally worn without socks.[1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"History","paras":["Sperry introduced the modern design in 1935.[1] Sailors wore them first; from the 1970s they spread as casual wear, trending in the 1980s and again in the late 2000s.[1] Their association with boat ownership gave them some status, and they appear in nautical and preppy fashion.[1] Some schools allow them because they are leather.[1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found."],"subs":[]}],"lore":null,"timeline":[{"year":"1935","event":"Paul Sperry invents the modern boat shoe.[1]"},{"year":"1970s","event":"Boat shoes become casual footwear in many coastal areas.[1]"},{"year":"1980s","event":"Trend peak; Sebago, Sperry and Eastland among the popular brands.[1]"},{"year":"Late 2000s","event":"Renewed popularity.[1]"}],"refs":[{"title":"Boat shoe","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boat_shoe","source":"Wikipedia","year":2025,"type":"encyclopedia"}],"studies":[],"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"Simo - The Red Shoe Diaries (Part 1)","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/simo-the-red-shoe-diaries-part-1/228734","site":"T Nation · 10000 posts · 2017"},{"title":"Things That Piss You Off","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/things-that-piss-you-off/163775","site":"T Nation · 7426 posts · 2011"},{"title":"GuineaPig’s Training Log - Hunt 300 Deadlift","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/guineapig-s-training-log-hunt-300-deadlift/235959","site":"T Nation · 6370 posts · 2017"},{"title":"The Tactical Life","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/the-tactical-life/232312","site":"T Na